"""
Section 6: Benchmark Results Template

Python string template that accepts benchmark data and renders:
- 6a: Raw Operation Benchmarks
- 6b: REST Cache-Aside Benchmarks
- 6c: Memory & GC Profiling

Includes Chart.js snippets for HTML output.
"""

BENCHMARK_TEMPLATE = """# 6. Benchmark Results

> **Methodology:** Each operation was measured over multiple iterations with a 10%
> warm-up phase. Latency percentiles (p50, p95, p99) are computed from individual
> operation timings. Throughput is calculated as operations per second from total
> elapsed time. All benchmarks run against a local 5-node Redis cluster.
> MGET/MSET are replaced with sequential GET/SET batches due to cross-slot
> restrictions in cluster mode.
>
> **Pipeline methodology:** C# `pipeline_100_gets` uses `CreateBatch` for true
> client-side pipelining — all 100 GETs are sent in a single batch before awaiting
> any responses. Haskell `sequential_100_gets` sends 100 individual GETs through
> the cluster multiplexer, each awaiting its response before sending the next.
> These test fundamentally different approaches: explicit batching vs. sequential
> operations over a multiplexed connection.

{benchmark_content}
"""

